[{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-1.1: its test AC_1_1_DisplaysReturnedImportPreviewFields does not prove the criterion (The preview mock contains only one purchase-order row, so add receiving and multiple-row fixtures/assertions to prove the listed fields are displayed for each returned record.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-1.2: its test AC_1_2_DisplaysSynchronizationCountsAndFailedRowDetails does not prove the criterion (The fixture has no failed row and asserts neither a failed row's source identifier nor its reported failure reason; include a failed outcome and assert both.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-2.1: its test AC_2_1_ShowsPurchaseOrderLineLotsPensAndCapacity does not prove the criterion (The lots response contains only one lot and the test does not exercise a purchase-order line mapped to multiple lots; use multiple assigned lots and assert each lot and pen's returned capacity and animal count.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-2.2: its test AC_2_2_ShowsUnresolvedRecordsAsUnavailableForPenOperations does not prove the criterion (The test checks generic unavailability and selector exclusion but not the affected source row, returned status and problem detail, or a capacity refusal and its limit/refused assignment; assert those applicable results.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-2.3: its test AC_2_3_ShowsDuplicateOutcomeWithoutAddingAnotherImportedRecord does not prove the criterion (The sync fixture's only row is an added row and no already-imported starting state is established, so the single identifier assertion does not prove a resynchronization displays the duplicate outcome without adding a second record.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-3.2: its test AC_3_2_RetainsSubmittedAssumptionsWithRefreshedForecast does not prove the criterion (The lot fixture has a measured ADG and the test does not assert that the refreshed forecast uses the configured default gain rate or displays a response associated with the submitted assumptions; set up no measured ADG and assert those returned forecast values.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-3.3: its test AC_3_3_ShowsReturnedSaleTimingRecommendationAndMetrics does not prove the criterion (The test covers only a sale-timing recommendation; add a feeding-adjustment response case and assert its recommendation and any supplied ADG, market-date, or plan-variance values.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-4.1: its test AC_4_1_ShowsInventoryItemDetailsAndStockMovementHistory does not prove the criterion (The inventory fixture contains only one item, so add multiple returned items and assert the required details and available stock values for each.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-4.2: its test AC_4_2_ShowsActualWastageSeparatelyFromConsumptionEstimates does not prove the criterion (The test checks the entered quantity, cause, consumption value, and ratio but does not assert that the returned movement is identified as actual wastage and displayed separately from consumption estimates; assert those distinct labels/values.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-5.1: its test AC_5_1_ShowsProjectedBalancesForEverySupportedHorizon does not prove the criterion (The handler returns the same weekly response for every horizon and the test only asserts one balance, horizon labels, and the ratio; return and assert each horizon's projected balance and ratio-reflecting consumption estimate.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-7.1: its test AC_7_1_ShowsFeasibleMixesWithNutritionAndCost does not prove the criterion (The test does not trigger an optimization request and its fixture has only one feasible mix, so it cannot prove returned mixes are displayed in lowest-cost order.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-7.2: its test AC_7_2_RequiresSelectingSuggestionBeforeUsingRation does not prove the criterion (The test does not assert that the suggestion is shown as unapplied before selection, or that the selected ration is displayed for use afterward.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-8.2: its test AC_8_2_DisplaysReturnedPlanStatus does not prove the criterion (The test checks only Planned and does not verify display of the other named returned statuses: In progress, Completed, and Skipped.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-9.3: its test AC_9_3_CollectsAndDisplaysSeparateQuantitiesForEachLot does not prove the criterion (Although it requires separate inputs, the test does not assert that each returned quantity is associated with its corresponding lot name.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-10.1: its test AC_10_1_DisplaysReturnedCostEnergyAndInventoryConsumption does not prove the criterion (The test checks values in the feeding-log screen after saving but does not open activity details or the affected inventory or lot views named by the criterion.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-10.2: its test AC_10_2_ShowsInventoryShortageWithoutSavingActivity does not prove the criterion (Checking only that Unplanned is absent does not establish that the activity is not shown as saved under another status or confirmation state.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-11.1: its test AC_11_1_ShowsReturnedWeightMeasurementAfterSave does not prove the criterion (The response repeats the submitted date, headcount, and average weight, so assert deliberately different mocked response values to distinguish returned data from an echoed form.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-11.2: its test AC_11_2_ShowsWeightHistoryInDateOrderWithReadingControls does not prove the criterion (The test orders readings by average-weight text and checks only a date header; assert both returned dates are visible and in chronological order.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-11.3: its test AC_11_3_ShowsReturnedSeriesAndRecalculatedMetricsAfterEdit does not prove the criterion (The edit response matches the original series and metrics, and the test omits deletion and validation-error cases; use changed returned data and assert the returned list and metrics for edit, delete, and error outcomes.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-12.1: its test AC_12_1_ShowsAllReturnedLotPerformanceMetrics does not prove the criterion (The test checks metric labels and expected numbers separately, so values could be shown under the wrong labels; assert each returned value alongside its corresponding metric label.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-12.2: its test AC_12_2_UsesAsFedPoundsAsFeedConversionRatioBasis does not prove the criterion (It verifies the as-fed total and an “as-fed” string but not that the displayed feed conversion ratio uses that total as its basis; assert that relationship explicitly.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-12.3: its test AC_12_3_ShowsReturnedTotalGainAndAverageDailyGain does not prove the criterion (The expected numbers are asserted independently of their labels, so assert the returned total gain and ADG values within their respective metric displays.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-12.4: its test AC_12_4_ShowsLatestMetricsAsSoonAsAWeightRecordIsSaved does not prove the criterion (This covers only saving a weight record and checks only gain and ADG; cover feeding and edit/delete outcomes too, and assert all latest returned feed-to-gain metrics without a manual recalculation step.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-14.1: its test AC_14_1_ShowsLotPenInventoryFeedAndPerformanceDashboardData does not prove the criterion (Most dashboard numbers are asserted without their metric labels or lot associations, so assert each required value with its corresponding label and identify which lots are best and worst performing.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-16.1: its test AC_16_1_ShowsFilteredFeedToGainRowsAndSelectedFilters does not prove the criterion (The mock contains only one lot and the assertions cover only rows[0], so use multiple returned lots and assert each lot and its metrics alongside the selected filters.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-16.2: its test AC_16_2_ShowsMetricsFromTheLatestWeightInTheSelectedRange does not prove the criterion (The single canned row cannot establish that the displayed weight is the latest one within the date range or that feed events after it are excluded, so add boundary readings and events and assert the resulting date and metrics.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-16.3: its test AC_16_3_ShowsTheReturnedFeedToGainFilterError does not prove the criterion (The mock returns 400 unconditionally after selecting the valid Angus option, so make the selected date range invalid or the filter unsupported before asserting the returned message.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-17.1: its test AC_17_1_DownloadsFilteredFeedToGainRowsAsCsv does not prove the criterion (The mock contains only one lot and the CSV assertions search only that row, so return multiple filtered rows and assert every displayed row and its metrics are included.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-18.1: its test AC_18_1_DownloadsFilteredFeedToGainRowsAsPdf does not prove the criterion (The mock contains only one lot and the test searches its text in a PDF-typed blob without validating a PDF document, so assert all rows from a multi-row filtered report in a valid downloadable PDF.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-19.2: its test AC_19_2_ShowsSeparateCountsAndDetailsForPartialDemoLoads does not prove the criterion (Record identifiers and reasons are searched in page-wide text without proving they appear under their matching added, already-present, and failed categories, so scope those assertions to each category.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-20.1: its test AC_20_1_DisplaysProjectSolutionArchitectureAndReadinessContent does not prove the criterion (The test searches for architecture-description text rather than asserting a displayed architecture diagram, so verify the diagram rendering as well as the required content sections.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-21.1: its test AC_21_1_ShowsTheSameOperationalViewsAndControlsInSeparateUserContexts does not prove the criterion (Both captures use the same routes and identical user context, so establish two distinct users or contexts before comparing their views and controls.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."}]